  "description": "Anonymous audit disclosures, one case per audit key and layout: commitment (class 4, two published inputs, both notes of the ring, no exit), commitment_exits (the same key with an exit) and entry (class 8, two published inputs, the second a default-ring note, with an exit). Encodings, fixed inputs, layout, the CRDS slot secret, the body and the exit blinding as in audit-disclosure-delivered.json, plus the domain tags CRRA, CRIK, CRIT, CRPK, CRPT. A ring output's tag is 31 bytes and its owner tag 0x00 || tag. An inbox tag is low248(Poseidon(CRIT, inbox_key, epoch, index)) with inbox_key = Poseidon(CRIK, ring_id, pack_be(0x04 || recipient_u)), a pair tag low248(Poseidon(CRPT, pair_key, epoch, index)) with pair_key = Poseidon(CRPK, first_contact_secret), a change tag low248 of tag_field, a dummy tag random. ring_secret = Poseidon(CRRA, slot_secret, 0x00 || tag), blinding = Poseidon(TXRB, n0, ring_secret, i). Every input belongs to the sender, owner Poseidon(owner identity of sender_key, sender_nullifier_pk), its data hashes zero, its commitment the UTXO hash under input_tree_id with ring id ring_id for a ring input and 0 for a default-ring input. plaintext: seed_out first when an output exits, then sender_nullifier_pk under the entry key, the nullifier_pk of every output (0 on a dummy), pack_disclosure(sender_key || one 64-byte slot per output, a ring output owner_key || recipient_u, an exit asset || u64be(amount) || 0^24, a dummy zeros), then under the commitment key the commitment of every published input, under the entry key pack_disclosure(u64be(amount) of all eight input slots, zero past the published inputs) and the asset and blinding of every published input. The auditor opens a commitment input among the notes it opened before. pad, published and disclosure_chain as in audit-disclosure.json. Generated by custom-rings/client/tests/disclosure_vectors.rs.",
